menu "Serial port task placement (advanced)"

    config SERIAL_PORT_DUAL_CORE
        bool "Enable dual-core task placement for UART receive tasks"
        default n
        help
            Pins the UART receive tasks (CAT to the radio, wired host link) to
            CPU1, isolating their jitter from BTstack's single-threaded run
            loop and SCO audio timing on CPU0.

            This option alone changes nothing: FREERTOS_NUMBER_OF_CORES /
            FREERTOS_UNICORE are system-level FreeRTOS settings that this app
            option cannot override. You must ALSO disable single-core mode
            yourself via Component config -> FreeRTOS. See the README section
            "Reparto de tareas entre nucleos" for the exact steps. If the
            firmware is still built in unicore mode, this option's effect is
            ignored at boot with a warning log; nothing breaks.

    config SERIAL_PORT_CAT_ON_CORE1
        bool "Pin the CAT (radio) UART task to core 1"
        depends on SERIAL_PORT_DUAL_CORE
        default y

    config SERIAL_PORT_HOST_SERIAL_ON_CORE1
        bool "Pin the wired host link (UART0) task to core 1"
        depends on SERIAL_PORT_DUAL_CORE
        default y

endmenu
